Krita Nova 23 - rounded undocked dockers and brush editor (Android)

Like the Brush Panel (patch 15), every docker gets rounded corners (8 px) and
a grey 1.5 px outline while it is undocked, and so does the brush editor
("Brush Settings") popup.

1. KisMainWindow::createDockWidget(): on Android, RoundedPanelPainter is
   installed on every docker. It paints only while the docker is a window of
   its own (floating); docked dockers look as before. The floating frame
   (at least 6 px, patch 14) keeps the docker's contents inside the rounded
   corners.
2. KisPopupButtonFrame (patch 11): on Android, a popup with a title bar has a
   translucent background and paints the rounded panel itself; the title
   bar no longer fills its own (square) background, and the frame has small
   margins so the contents stay inside the corners.

